        "abstract": "As part of a project concerned with the high-voltage impulse response of concentrated earth electrodes, the electrical breakdown and ionization processes in soil were investigated. Two processes, namely corona and streamer discharges occur in soil. Streamers are associated with exceptionally long time delays and a velocity and impedance which can depend on a number of factors, for instance the field strength, soil type and the electrode geometry. Even if these processes were fully understood, a mathematical model would be too cumbersome for engineering applications, and the use of the alternative “uniform ionization zone” model is illusrated for spherical electrodes. It is suggested that only results of tests on practical outdoor electrodes be used when assessing the soil parameters to be used with this model.",
