        "abstract": "While much effort has been directed towards the modelling of the breakdown behaviour of airgaps, the stage has not yet been reached where predicted behaviour is of sufficient accuracy to completely replace measured behaviour. The one area posing the most difficulties is in the determination of the low probability region of the probability of breakdown vs voltage characteristic. The use of the multiple-gap technique for measurement in this region has been proposed by previous reseachers. This paper describes an experimental approach for testing the validity of the multiple-gap technique that is more rigorous than previous attempts. This paper was presented at the Fifth International Symposium on High Voltage Engineering. Braunschweig, West Germany and is published with permission.",
