                "firstName": "J D",
                "lastName": "van Wyk"
            }
        ],
        "abstract": "The fundamental definitions of power are critically reviewed on the basis of establishing proper measurement and deriving proper distortion compensation criteria, in power systems with non-sinusoidal and in general aperiodic currents and voltages. A time-domain definition of power, using correlation techniques, is proposed. A combination between digital- and analogue signal processing techniques are proposed in the measurement and analysis of the components of power. Adaptive estimation of network parameters is investigated in the control loops of dynamic power filters, necessary in compensation of fictitious power. Results of simulated and practical power measurements and on an experimental electronic Pulse Width Modulated power converter, used in fictitious power compensation, are included in this paper.",
